Which code produces a value of this hybrid type without any type assertion?

```ts
interface Counter {
  (start: number): string;
  interval: number;
  reset(): void;
}
```

What does TypeScript report for the last line?

```ts
interface Counter {
  (start: number): string;
  interval: number;
  reset(): void;
}

const c3 = (start: number) => String(start);
c3.interval = 1;
const bad: Counter = c3;
```

Which two calls compile? (Choose two.)

```ts
class Point {
  constructor(x: number, y: number);
  constructor(coords: [number, number]);
  constructor(a: number | [number, number], b?: number) {
    /* … */
  }
}
```

Why does tsc report TS2394 ("This overload signature is not compatible with its implementation signature") on the second overload?

```ts
class Q {
  constructor(x: number, y: number);
  constructor(coords: [number, number]);
  constructor(a: number, b?: number) {}
}
```

What is `P`?

```ts
class Point {
  constructor(x: number, y: number);
  constructor(coords: [number, number]);
  constructor(a: number | [number, number], b?: number) {
    /* … */
  }
}

type P = ConstructorParameters<typeof Point>;
```

With `"strict": true`, tsc reports nothing for this code, yet `save` can reject and nobody handles it. Which tool flags the un-awaited call?

```ts
async function save() { /* may throw */ }

async function run() {
  save();
}
```

What happens here?

```ts
interface A { id: string }
interface B { id: number }

interface C extends A, B {}
type D = A & B;
```

What does `C` resolve to?

```ts
type Shape =
  | { kind: "circle"; r: number }
  | { kind: "square"; s: number };

type C = Extract<Shape, { kind: "circle" }>;
```

Why does the last line fail?

```ts
abstract class Animal { abstract speak(): string }
class Dog extends Animal { speak() { return "woof"; } }

function create<K extends new () => any>(k: K): InstanceType<K> {
  return new k();
}

create(Dog);
create(Animal);
```

What does this log?

```ts
class Animal { speak() { return "..."; } }
class Cat extends Animal { speak() { return "meow"; } }

const a: Animal = new Cat();
console.log(a.speak());
```

Why does tsc report TS2855 on the `super.handle()` call?

```ts
class H1 {
  handle = () => "base";
  method() { return "m"; }
}
class H2 extends H1 {
  handle = () => super.handle();
  method() { return super.method() + "!"; }
}
```

Why does the first line fail while the second compiles?

```ts
const a = "42" as number;
const b = "42" as unknown as number;
```
